These operations stop and restart the DMA ring without serialization. If multiple timeout-triggered calls to `hci_dma_dequeue_xfer()` execute concurrently, the ring state can be corrupted: one call may abort the ring while another already did, or one may restart the ring before another finishes processing, leading to inconsistent ring behavior.

